<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Ouchy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1912">1912</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as First Treaty of Lausanne · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italo-turkish-war">Italo-Turkish War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Ouchy, signed at Ouchy near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lausanne">Lausanne</a> on 18 October 1912, ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italo-turkish-war">Italo-Turkish War</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> withdrew its forces and officials from Tripolitania and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrenaica">Cyrenaica</a>, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> had already annexed as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a>. Italy was to hand back the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dodecanese">Dodecanese</a> islands once the Ottomans left Libya, but it kept them, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a> recognised Italian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> over them in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-lausanne">Treaty of Lausanne</a> of 1923.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-ouchy.jpg" alt="Treaty of Ouchy" width="320" height="314" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: File:Turkish prisoners Rhodes 1912.jpg: L'Illustrazione italiana, 16 June 1912. File:Atatürk 1912.jpg: Bilinmiyor Fil... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Italo-Turkish_war_collage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
